-- title:
--   Finite étale local extensions of complete regular two-dimensional local rings
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a regular local ring, complete with respect to its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$ in the sense that $R$ is $\mathfrak m_R$-adically complete (Hausdorff and complete), and suppose there are elements $\varpi, s \in R$ with $\mathfrak m_R = (\varpi, s)$, while the Krull dimension of $R$, as an element of $\mathbb{Z}_{\ge -\infty}$-valued `ringKrullDim`, equals $2$. Let $R_1$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an $R$-algebra structure which makes it module-finite over $R$ and étale over $R$ (formally unramified and of finite presentation as an $R$-algebra). The conclusion is the conjunction of four assertions: $R_1$ is a regular local ring; its Krull dimension is again $2$; its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_{R_1}$ is the ideal generated by the images $\varpi\cdot 1$ and $s \cdot 1$ of $\varpi$ and $s$ under the structure map $R \to R_1$, so the pair $(\varpi,s)$ remains a system of generators; and $R_1$ is $\mathfrak m_{R_1}$-adically complete. No separatedness or connectedness hypothesis beyond locality of $R_1$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard transfer of regularity, dimension, the regular system of parameters and adic completeness along a module-finite étale local extension of a complete regular two-dimensional local ring. It serves as the shape statement used when one passes to rings of the form $\hat S^{I}$ for an inertia subgroup, or adjoins roots of unity, in the Abhyankar-type arguments at a smooth point, and is cited in the constructions of étale local extensions containing primitive roots of unity, of Galois cyclic tensor decompositions, and of ring isomorphisms with adic completions of invariant subrings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_of_etale_of_isLocalRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open IsLocalRing Polynomial

universe u v

theorem IsRegularLocalRing.of_etale_of_isLocalRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R]
    (ϖ s : R) (hmax : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {ϖ, s}) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = 2)
    (R₁ : Type v) [CommRing R₁] [IsLocalRing R₁] [Algebra R R₁] [Module.Finite R R₁] [Algebra.Etale R R₁] :
    IsRegularLocalRing R₁ ∧ ringKrullDim R₁ = 2 ∧
      maximalIdeal R₁ = Ideal.span {algebraMap R R₁ ϖ, algebraMap R R₁ s} ∧
      IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R₁) R₁ := by sorry
